course: dictionary
lesson: 5008
title: What is an infection?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An infection is an illness caused by tiny germs getting into your body. The germs may be bacteria, viruses or fungi. «A graze scrapes off the top layer of skin, and dirt left in it can cause an infection.» The dirt carries germs into the cut, and they can make it red, swollen and sore.
explain: Infection can also mean germs spreading from one person or thing to another. That is why we wash our hands, do not share cups, and cover our coughs. Each of these stops germs moving from person to person.
explain: Your body often fights back. «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection.» A normal body temperature is about 36.5 to 37.5 degrees Celsius. If you have a fever or a cut that looks infected, tell an adult.
fact: An infection is an illness caused by germs such as bacteria, viruses or fungi.
fact: Infection can also mean germs spreading from one person or thing to another.
fact: Antibiotics can treat some infections caused by bacteria, but they do not work on viruses like colds.
fact: Signs of an infected cut include redness spreading, swelling, heat or pus, so tell an adult.
fact: You can help prevent infection by washing your hands, covering cuts, covering coughs and not sharing cups.
exercise: «A graze scrapes off the top layer of skin, and dirt left in it can cause an infection.» What can cause an infection in a graze? | Wearing a bright plaster | Eating a healthy breakfast | The sun shining on the graze | *Dirt with germs left in the cut
exercise: Which sign shows a cut may be infected? | A smooth, clean scab with no colour | *Redness spreading, swelling and heat | Cold, dry skin | Growing taller
exercise: Which action helps stop infection spreading? | Sharing your cup with a friend | Sneezing into your hand and then shaking hands | *Washing your hands before eating | Leaving a cut open to the air
test: Why does the body have a fever? | *To help fight infection | To make you sleepy for a whole week | To make your skin shiny | Because it is cold outside
test: Antibiotics can treat some infections. Which illness will they NOT work on? | A chest infection caused by bacteria | *A cold caused by a virus | An infection caused by bacteria
exam: «Swimmer's ear is an infection of the ear canal, outside the eardrum.» Where is swimmer's ear? | *The ear canal, outside the eardrum | On the knee | Deep inside the brain | Inside the nose
